# `**/.klauro*` / `apps/mcp-server/.klauro-*` above (meant to keep local
# analyzer caches out of the image) also matched deploy.sh's own
# .klauro-build-stamp.json, silently dropping it from every Docker build
# context — deploy.sh wrote a real git sha to this file on the VPS host
# before `docker compose build`, but the file never reached the image, so
# apps/api/Dockerfile's COPY apps/mcp-server step always shipped a container
# with no stamp, and build-identity.ts's getBuildIdentity() fell back to
# "unknown" regardless of which deploy path was used. Re-include it.
!apps/mcp-server/.klauro-build-stamp.json
